# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# Internal architecture notes, deliberately not tracked. `tests/concepts.rs` (M0) guards
# them and skips when the directory is absent, which is what CI sees.
#
# The third-party corpus — the Blue and Green Book excerpts, IEC 62056 sample pages, the
# P1 companion standards — lives at `concepts/reference/` and is covered by this line:
# DLMS UA / IEC copyrighted material, not redistributable, indexed in
# `concepts/REFERENCES.md`.
/concepts/
# Its predecessor: a single unlinked design document, split into concepts/. Kept ignored
# so it cannot come back by accident.
CONCEPT.md

# This project's own feature specifications, and the Spec Kit machinery that produces
# them: one `specs/NNN-slug/` per ROADMAP item, `.specify/memory/constitution.md`, the
# threatspec extension, and the `/speckit-*` skills. Same rule as `concepts/` — internal,
# and the published tree may not cite a path its reader does not have;
# scripts/concepts-check.sh fails on one that does. Matching eebus, ocpp-kit and sepa.
/specs/
/.specify/
/.claude/
.DS_Store

# The documentation site is built from `site/` by Zola; the output is not tracked.
/site/public/

# Fuzzing corpora and artifacts
/fuzz/target/
/fuzz/corpus/
/fuzz/artifacts/
/fuzz/coverage/
